    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0809" n="713" xml:id="pg713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-07T18:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 7—5:32
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>265. Legation at Peking sends following telegram to be repeated to Department as
                    its no. 282, August 7, noon.</p>
                <p>Japan now ready to negotiate, says Yourin.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d659-f1"/> Form
                    of negotiations dependent upon American interest in them. Yourin will have to
                    concede more if the United States does not take such interest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d659-f1" n="17" xml:id="d659-f1-content">
                <p>Ignatius Yurin, president of the mission of the Far Eastern Republic to
                    China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
